                <pb facs="1105" n="1093" sameAs="frus:frus1946v08/pg1093"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">892.014/10–1846: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Caffery</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-10-18T18:00:00+01:00">October 18, 1946—6
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received October 18—4:24 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>5258. Bidault asked me this afternoon to convey to my Government and especially
                    to the Secretary of State the high appreciation <pb facs="1106" n="1094"
                        xml:id="pg1094"/> of his Government for the respective help given by the
                    Department of State in connection with the nullification of the 1941 agreement
                    and the Siamese decision to return to Indochina the four disputed provinces. He
                    said that his Government is fully aware that without our assistance this action
                    would never have been taken by the Siamese Government.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Caffery</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
